  "rationale": "The workflow runs dotnet restore and dotnet tool restore on every matrix job (six OS/configuration combinations) without caching the NuGet package cache, so dependencies are re-fetched on each run. Pattern P-LIT-GHA-CACHE reports that caching dependency downloads saves CI resources (reported modest aggregate benefit, about 6% free / 3.4% paid VM time), and its preconditions are met here: repeated dependency fetching is measurable, and the cache key can include the lockfile/csproj inputs plus runner OS. Adding actions/cache for ~/.nuget/packages after checkout and before restore preserves every build and test step and all coverage/publish behavior, adds no secrets or privileged actions, and does not introduce new network access (it reduces repeated fetches from nuget.org).",
